# Loaded by `vite dev` (development mode). Committed on purpose — these are the
# LOCAL dev endpoints, no secrets. For personal overrides use
# `.env.development.local` (gitignored), NOT `.env.local`: Vite's order is
# `.env` < `.env.local` < `.env.[mode]` < `.env.[mode].local`, so this file
# already beats `.env.local` and an override put there is silently ignored.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://localhost:55321
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJleHAiOjE5ODM4MTI5OTZ9.CRXP1A7WOeoJeXxjNni43kdQwgnWNReilDMblYTn_I0
# The dev proxy target (vite.config.ts reads this; in dev the browser itself is
# same-origin and never sees it — see API_ORIGIN in src/lib/api.ts).
#
# This is the LOCAL backend, on purpose. A Cloudflare quick-tunnel URL used to
# live here and the comment above it already said tunnels belong in a local
# override — but the tunnel stayed committed, went dead, and every fresh clone
# inherited a broken dev proxy with no clue why. A value that is EXPECTED to
# change every session cannot be the one in git: the committed default has to be
# the thing that works out of the box, and the churning value has to be opt-in.
#
# To point at a tunnel (or any remote backend) instead, either:
#   1. `.env.development.local` — `VITE_API_URL=https://<your>.trycloudflare.com`.
#      Gitignored via `.gitignore`'s `.env.*.local`, and Vite loads it AFTER this
#      file, so it wins. This is the durable per-developer route.
#   2. a shell override — `VITE_API_URL=https://… npm run dev`. Highest
#      precedence of all, and dies with the shell. Good for one-off sessions.
# Either way the value must still parse as a URL (src/lib/env.ts: `z.url()`).
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
# RevenueCat Web Billing SANDBOX key — checkout runs in Stripe Test Mode, so
# purchases use test cards (4242 4242 4242 4242) and never charge real money.
VITE_REVENUECAT_WEB_BILLING_KEY=rcb_sb_jrhhpHgvWGFReNIsCRkHHTfZu
